    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0447" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.124A/20: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wharton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-27T18:00:00-05:00">December 27, 1929—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>57. Your December 23, 6 p.m. Form of Article 3 as changed by Barclay
                    satisfactory.</p>
                <p>For your information Dr. Smith of Public Health Service sails for Monrovia from
                    Rotterdam on January 3.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d363-f1"/> (See Department’s
                    telegram No. 37, October 8, 1929, Paragraph 5 (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >e</hi>).)</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d363-f1" n="47" xml:id="d363-f1-content">
                <p>Arrived at Monrovia on January 20, 1930. His appointment was approved by
                    President Hoover on December 5, 1929.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
